      "committer_account_type": "User",
      "message": "Add Foundry docs llms.txt with Context7 config and weekly update workflow\n\n- Add scraper to generate llms.txt from Microsoft Learn TOC API (261 pages)\n- Add context7.json for Context7 library submission\n- Add gh-aw workflow for weekly automated updates via PR\n- Include llms-full.txt with expanded content",
      "parent_shas": [
        "e276ccbf281534abec4431a319e04d31dcd6909b"
      ],
      "tree_sha": "35a2e535d3900dc2f2ba2b7be5deca7af7735077",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/microsoft/skills/commit/5d0053512f616b9be054c90716fc9a12f2fd2afd",
      "verification_verified": true,
      "verification_reason": "valid",
      "actor_type": "human",
      "attribution_class": "human_no_agent_signal",
      "agent_name": "",
      "attribution_confidence": "operational_label",
      "attribution_evidence": "no supported agent signature in commit metadata",
      "md_changes": [
        {
          "source_key": "microsoft/skills:.github/workflows/update-llms-txt.md",
          "source_full_name": "microsoft/skills",
          "md_path": ".github/workflows/update-llms-txt.md",
          "commit_sha": "5d0053512f616b9be054c90716fc9a12f2fd2afd",
          "committed_at": "2026-01-19T18:07:27Z",
          "event_status": "added",
          "previous_path": "",
          "file_additions": 51,
          "file_deletions": 0,
          "file_changes": 51,
          "file_patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@\n+---\n+on:\n+  schedule: weekly\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+  issues: read\n+  pull-requests: read\n+network: defaults\n+tools:\n+  github:\n+  bash: [\"python3\", \"pip\", \"git\", \"diff\"]\n+safe-outputs:\n+  create-pull-request:\n+    title-prefix: \"[docs-update] \"\n+    labels: [automated, documentation]\n+---\n+\n+# Update Foundry llms.txt Documentation\n+\n+Regenerate the llms.txt and llms-full.txt files from the latest Microsoft Foundry documentation.\n+\n+## Purpose\n+\n+This workflow keeps our Foundry documentation index up-to-date by:\n+1. Fetching the latest Table of Contents from Microsoft Learn\n+2. Regenerating llms.txt with current documentation links\n+3. Creating a PR if there are changes\n+\n+## Steps\n+\n+1. **Setup Python environment**\n+   - Install required packages: `pip install aiohttp`\n+\n+2. **Run the scraper**\n+   - Execute `python scripts/scrape_foundry_docs.py` to regenerate llms.txt\n+   - Execute `python scripts/generate_llms_full.py` to regenerate llms-full.txt\n+\n+3. **Check for changes**\n+   - Compare the generated files with the existing ones\n+   - If there are changes, create a pull request with the updates\n+\n+4. **Create PR if needed**\n+   - Title: \"Update Foundry llms.txt documentation\"\n+   - Include summary of what changed (new pages, removed pages, section changes)\n+\n+## Notes\n+\n+- The scraper respects rate limits when fetching from Microsoft Learn\n+- Only creates a PR if there are actual content changes\n+- The llms.txt follows the llms.txt specification for LLM-friendly documentation",
          "snapshot_ref": "5d0053512f616b9be054c90716fc9a12f2fd2afd",
